{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Building a Tokenizer from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Byte-Level Encoding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The foundation. Convert any string into a sequence of bytes, map each byte to a printable character for display, and reverse the process."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bytes_to_tokens(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return list(text.encode(\"utf-8\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tokens_to_text(token_bytes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return bytes(token_bytes).decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Test on multilingual text to see the byte counts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "texts = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"English\", \"hello\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"Chinese\", \"\u4f60\u597d\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"Emoji\", \"\ud83d\udd25\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"Mixed\", \"hello\u4f60\u597d\ud83d\udd25\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for label, text in texts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b = bytes_to_tokens(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{label}: {len(text)} chars -> {len(b)} bytes -> {b}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\"hello\" is 5 bytes. \"\u4f60\u597d\" is 6 bytes (3 per character). The fire emoji is 4 bytes. The byte-level tokenizer does not care what language it is. Bytes are bytes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Pre-Tokenizer with Regex"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split text into chunks using the GPT-2 regex pattern. Each chunk gets tokenized independently by BPE."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import re"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "try:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    import regex"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    GPT2_PATTERN = regex.compile("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        r\"\"\"'(?:[sdmt]|ll|ve|re)| ?\\p{L}+| ?\\p{N}+| ?[^\\s\\p{L}\\p{N}]+|\\s+(?!\\S)|\\s+\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "except ImportError:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    GPT2_PATTERN = re.compile("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        r\"\"\"'(?:[sdmt]|ll|ve|re)| ?[a-zA-Z]+| ?[0-9]+| ?[^\\s\\w]+|\\s+(?!\\S)|\\s+\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def pre_tokenize(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [match.group() for match in GPT2_PATTERN.finditer(text)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `regex` module supports Unicode property escapes (`\\p{L}` for letters, `\\p{N}` for numbers). The standard library `re` module does not, so we fall back to ASCII character classes. For production multilingual tokenizers, install `regex`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Try it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(pre_tokenize(\"Hello, world! Don't stop.\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# [' Hello', ',', ' world', '!', \" Don\", \"'t\", ' stop', '.']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The leading space stays attached to the word. Contractions split at the apostrophe. Punctuation becomes its own chunk. BPE will never merge tokens across these boundaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: BPE on Byte Sequences"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core algorithm from Lesson 01, but now operating on pre-tokenized chunks independently."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def get_byte_pairs(chunks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pairs = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for chunk in chunks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        byte_seq = list(chunk.encode(\"utf-8\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(byte_seq) - 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pairs[(byte_seq[i], byte_seq[i + 1])] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return pairs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def apply_merge(byte_seq, pair, new_id):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    merged = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    i = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while i < len(byte_seq):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if i < len(byte_seq) - 1 and byte_seq[i] == pair[0] and byte_seq[i + 1] == pair[1]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            merged.append(new_id)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            i += 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            merged.append(byte_seq[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            i += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return merged"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Special Token Handling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Special tokens need exact matching and fixed IDs. They bypass BPE entirely."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SpecialTokenHandler:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.special_tokens = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pattern = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def add_token(self, token_str, token_id):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.special_tokens[token_str] = token_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        escaped = [re.escape(t) for t in sorted(self.special_tokens.keys(), key=len, reverse=True)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pattern = re.compile(\"|\".join(escaped))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def split_with_specials(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not self.pattern:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return [(text, False)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        parts = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        last_end = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for match in self.pattern.finditer(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if match.start() > last_end:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                parts.append((text[last_end:match.start()], False))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            parts.append((match.group(), True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            last_end = match.end()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if last_end < len(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            parts.append((text[last_end:], False))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return parts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Full Tokenizer Class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Chain everything together: normalize, split on special tokens, pre-tokenize, BPE merge, map to IDs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import unicodedata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ProductionTokenizer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.merges = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vocab = {i: bytes([i]) for i in range(256)}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.special_handler = SpecialTokenHandler()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.next_id = 256"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def normalize(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKC\", text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, text, num_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        text = self.normalize(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks = pre_tokenize(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunk_bytes = [list(chunk.encode(\"utf-8\")) for chunk in chunks]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(num_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pairs = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for seq in chunk_bytes:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(len(seq) - 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    pairs[(seq[j], seq[j + 1])] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if not pairs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best = max(pairs, key=pairs.get)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            new_id = self.next_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.next_id += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.merges[best] = new_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.vocab[new_id] = self.vocab[best[0]] + self.vocab[best[1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunk_bytes = [apply_merge(seq, best, new_id) for seq in chunk_bytes]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def add_special_token(self, token_str):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        token_id = self.next_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.next_id += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.special_handler.add_token(token_str, token_id)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vocab[token_id] = token_str.encode(\"utf-8\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return token_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def encode(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        text = self.normalize(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        parts = self.special_handler.split_with_specials(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        all_ids = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for part_text, is_special in parts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if is_special:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                all_ids.append(self.special_handler.special_tokens[part_text])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for chunk in pre_tokenize(part_text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    byte_seq = list(chunk.encode(\"utf-8\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    for pair, new_id in self.merges.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        byte_seq = apply_merge(byte_seq, pair, new_id)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    all_ids.extend(byte_seq)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return all_ids"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def decode(self, ids):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        byte_parts = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token_id in ids:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if token_id in self.vocab:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                byte_parts.append(self.vocab[token_id])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return b\"\".join(byte_parts).decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def vocab_size(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(self.vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Multilingual Test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The real test. Throw English, Chinese, emoji, and code at it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "corpus = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"The quick brown fox runs through the forest. \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"Machine learning models process natural language. \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"Deep learning transforms how we build software. \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"def train(model, data): return model.fit(data) \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"def predict(model, x): return model(x) \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tok = ProductionTokenizer()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tok.train(corpus, num_merges=50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bos = tok.add_special_token(\"<|begin|>\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "eos = tok.add_special_token(\"<|end|>\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "test_texts = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"The quick brown fox.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\u4f60\u597d\u4e16\u754c\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"Hello \ud83c\udf0d World\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"def foo(x): return x + 1\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    f\"<|begin|>Hello<|end|>\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for text in test_texts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ids = tok.encode(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    decoded = tok.decode(ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
